  "cards":[
    {"dot":"cyan","title":"The model proposes; handlers act","items":["The browser registers context and tools. Native handlers call shared workflow commands or authenticated domain APIs.","The illustrated messages are a logical sequence, not a captured runtime trace. Local reads may need no HTTP call."]},
    {"dot":"violet","title":"Which model answers?","items":["Sina uses the configured Replit or Vercel gateway and OPENAI_CHAT_MODEL (code default: gpt-4o). Live configuration was not inspected.","MicroSina uses a version-pinned Foundry agent. The adapter's gpt-5 string is a serialization hint, not proof of its deployed model."]},
    {"dot":"rose","title":"Conditions matter","items":["Server checks apply again to each domain call. Workflow writes can require review or a matching scoped grant.","Mkoro is optional: the personal companion polls and runs Goose locally. Native workflow and source ownership stays in the platform.","Foundry public toolbox access is optional and defaults off; this diagram does not assert it is enabled."]}
